# Review requirements, weighted by blast radius.
#
# Most of this repository is documentation and declarative configuration, where
# a mistake is visible and reversible. Four paths are different: they define
# what executes on a host, and a mistake in them runs everywhere before anyone
# reads it. Those get a named reviewer, and branch protection should require
# review from a code owner so that the requirement is enforced rather than
# advisory.

*                       @dlapiduz

# The execution paths — see docs/06-provenance.md.
/endpoint/              @dlapiduz
/scripts/               @dlapiduz
/ansible/               @dlapiduz
/terraform/fleet/       @dlapiduz

# The trust roots themselves. Changing who may sign, or what CI checks, is a
# change to every guarantee downstream of it.
/.allowed_signers       @dlapiduz
/.github/               @dlapiduz
